---
import BlockLayout from '../layouts/BlockLayout.astro';
import { DEVNET, assertDevnetLaunchPinned } from '../data/chain-home';
assertDevnetLaunchPinned();
---
<BlockLayout title="Explore PointCast Chain V2" description="Practice a chain receipt, then inspect a real public devnet example." hideAds>
  <main class="pilot" data-pilot data-api={DEVNET.url} data-genesis={DEVNET.genesis} data-chain-id={DEVNET.chainId}>
    <nav><a href="/chain/">← PointCast Chain</a> <a href="/chain/plan/">The launch plan</a></nav>
    <header><p class="eyebrow">V2 EXPLORATION · EXISTING EXPERIMENTAL DEVNET</p><h1>A first look at V2.</h1><p class="lead">Try a tiny practice action, then follow a real transaction from the public test network.</p><p>This is an interface exploration using the existing devnet. It does not launch a new chain or change the protocol.</p></header>
    <p class="notice"><strong>This is a test network, not a mainnet.</strong> One operator runs the server. It can pause or reset; its play balances have no promised value. Public chain data is unmoderated. A server's report is not independent proof.</p>
    <section aria-labelledby="practice-title"><p class="eyebrow">01 · PRIVATE PRACTICE</p><h2 id="practice-title">Make a practice receipt</h2><p>Press the button to see what a receipt looks like. This happens only in this page: no account, key, payment, personal information or chain write.</p><button type="button" data-practice>Make a practice receipt</button><div class="result" data-practice-result role="status" aria-live="polite"></div></section>
    <section aria-labelledby="example-title"><p class="eyebrow">02 · PUBLIC EXAMPLE</p><h2 id="example-title">Inspect a real transaction</h2><p>Read an existing example from the devnet. The server reports the transaction and block; the next steps help you inspect the receipt and check the block yourself.</p><button type="button" data-find>Find an example</button><p data-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><div class="result" data-example hidden><p><strong>Transaction hash</strong><br /><code data-hash tabindex="0"></code></p><button type="button" data-copy>Copy hash</button><p><strong>Reported block</strong> <span data-height></span></p><p>The node reports this transaction as included. It is an observation, not proof of finality.</p><ol><li>Copy the hash above, open <a href="/chain/receipt/">Receipt Desk</a>, paste it and choose <strong>Check transaction</strong>.</li><li>Open <a href="/chain/verify-a-block/">Verify a block</a> and enter the reported block number. That lesson checks block data in your browser, but it can skip unsupported transaction types and does not by itself prove this hash was included.</li></ol><p class="fine">The receipt lookup and block checker may be unavailable or disagree if the network resets or changes. No query is added to these links.</p></div></section>
    <section aria-labelledby="limits-title"><p class="eyebrow">03 · BEFORE PUBLIC WRITES</p><h2 id="limits-title">What comes next?</h2><p>Writing from this page is deliberately unavailable while the operator verifies backups and restore, public-write limits, abuse handling, monitoring and an emergency stop. Practice is not a chain transaction. <a href="/chain/plan/">Read the dated launch plan →</a></p></section>
    <noscript><p>JavaScript is needed for the practice and live example. You can still open <a href="/chain/receipt/">Receipt Desk</a> or <a href="/chain/verify-a-block/">Verify a block</a>.</p></noscript>
  </main>
  <script is:inline type="module" src="/chain/apps/pilot.js"></script>
</BlockLayout>
<style>
.pilot{max-width:980px;margin:auto;padding:clamp(20px,5vw,60px);font:1rem/1.6 system-ui,sans-serif;color:#23332e}.pilot *{box-sizing:border-box}.pilot nav{display:flex;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap}.pilot a{color:#175e4a}.pilot header{padding:52px 0 24px}.pilot h1{font:400 clamp(2.7rem,7vw,5rem)/1.05 Georgia,serif;letter-spacing:-.04em;margin:12px 0}.pilot h2{font:400 clamp(1.8rem,4vw,2.5rem)/1.15 Georgia,serif;margin:0}.pilot .lead{font-size:1.15rem;max-width:600px}.pilot .eyebrow{font-size:.72rem;letter-spacing:.12em;font-weight:750;color:#29694f}.pilot .notice{padding:18px;background:#fff3db;border-left:4px solid #b57a37}.pilot section{padding:30px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #d5dfd7}.pilot button{min-height:48px;padding:11px 18px;background:#225c49;color:white;border:0;border-radius:6px;font:inherit;font-weight:700;cursor:pointer}.pilot button:disabled{opacity:.65;cursor:wait}.pilot :is(a,button):focus-visible{outline:3px solid #c37c2f;outline-offset:3px}.pilot .result:not(:empty){margin-top:20px;padding:18px;background:#edf4ee;border:1px solid #cbded0;border-radius:8px}.pilot [hidden]{display:none!important}.pilot code{overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word;font-size:.85rem}.pilot .fine{font-size:.85rem;color:#53665c}@media(max-width:480px){.pilot header{padding-top:35px}.pilot button{width:100%}}
</style>
